#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""media-dept-baseline -- the Media Department's M0 measured baseline (idp#7395, charter v1 §7 M0).

WHY. The charter forbids building a department on what the estate is assumed to have: "never infer
deployment from YAML". So before any runtime, this measures what exists for the department's remit
(film, director, scene contract, Fleet/Face, research engine, authorization door, orchestrators) and
writes a capability matrix where every cell came from a command that is recorded beside it.

WHAT IT WRITES. docs/departments/media/m0-capability-matrix.json, one row per capability:

    implemented    true/false   every named path exists at the source sha (git cat-file)
    tested         pass/fail/unknown/none   the row's test files, run here when --run-tests
    ci_wired       true/false   a workflow on the source sha runs those tests
    observed_live  observed/not_observed/blind   a real runtime observation; BLIND when no
                                instrument can reach the runtime (the OKE cluster, 2026-10-29)
    broken         true/false   a test failed, or a required contract is missing
    unknown        [...]        the fields that could not be measured, each with why

plus a ranked gap list. A gap is emitted only when its precondition holds on the measured rows,
so a gap that has been closed drops out on the next run instead of rotting in a document.

    bin/media-dept-baseline                 # measure origin/main, no live probes, no test runs
    bin/media-dept-baseline --run-tests     # also run each row's Python tests locally
    bin/media-dept-baseline --live          # also probe the cluster and the laptop director
    bin/media-dept-baseline --check         # exit 1 if the committed matrix fails its invariants

Go tests are not run here: on 2026-10-29 one `go test ./internal/director/` build on the founder's
laptop took the disk from 438 MiB free to full, so the director row reports `tested: unknown` with
that reason, and its CI wiring is measured instead.
"""

from __future__ import annotations

import argparse
import hashlib
import json
import re
import subprocess
import sys
from datetime import datetime, timezone
from pathlib import Path

IDP = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
OUT = IDP / "docs" / "departments" / "media" / "m0-capability-matrix.json"

